        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_984589535.1",
        "comments": "The assembly drSpiSali1.hap1.1 is based on 41x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The genome resolves into 18 homologous chromosome pairs, submitted as haplotype 1 and haplotype 2. Additional homology between chromosome pairs suggests allotetraploidy, consistent with the reported chromosome number for Spiraea salicifolia (2n=36; Oginuma, Tatarenko & Kondo, 2004). A haplotypic inversion was observed in the region on chromosome 14 (7,463 ? 8,650 & 8,664 ? 9,809 Kbp). A haplotypic inversion was observed in the region on chromosome 16 (4,593 - 6,5,30 Kbp).",
